  All Rights Reserved.

  https://paskalcpp.org

  SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0 WITH AdditionRef-PaskalCPP-Runtime-Exception

  This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the
  Mozilla Public License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL
  was not distributed with this file, You can obtain one
  at https://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.

  This file is covered by the PaskalCPP Runtime Exception
  (RUNTIME-EXCEPTION.md).
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  sfml_ext.pcpp - SFML extensions: `import sfml_ext;` adds namespace sfx to
  SFML 3 (it imports sfml). Used exactly as SFML's own types are, sf:: values
  in and out; the plain sf:: API stays usable beside them.

  sfx::RenderWindow is an sf::RenderWindow (every sf::RenderWindow call works
  on it) with what SFML 3 lacks:
    - DPI scaling: the window is created at its base (logical) size x the
      monitor's scale (DPI / 96), centred on the work area, and follows a DPI
      change (Windows: per monitor; Linux: X11's Xft.dpi, 96 when unset).
    - A letterbox frame: startFrame() draws in base-size coordinates whatever
      the window's size; the aspect is kept, bars outside it.
    - The mouse in frame coordinates, the frame rate, the program's own icon
      (the icon @exeicon gives the exe: Windows its stamped icon, Linux the
      picture built in as the data entry pcpp/exeicon; setIcon still works).
    - Window states: toggleFullscreen() (a borderless window over the
      monitor), setBordersVisible(), minimize() / maximize() / restore() and
      their queries (Windows: Win32; Linux: EWMH and Motif hints over X11).
    - Draw helpers: lines, polylines, rectangles, circles, ellipses,
      triangles and polygons (outlined at a thickness or filled), and text
      that stays crisp at any scale.
  display() hides sf::Window::display() (C++ name hiding): it adds the DPI
  follow and the frame timing. Called through an sf::Window it is SFML's.

  sfx::toSf() / fromSf() convert Math's geometry and Console's colour to
  SFML's and back, part for part: Math.Vector2 <-> sf::Vector2f, Math.Rect
  <-> sf::FloatRect, Console.Rgb <-> sf::Color (fromSf drops the alpha,
  toSf gives an opaque colour).

  sfx::ZipStream is an sf::InputStream over one entry of a .zip archive, with
  or without its password: sf::Font / sf::Texture / sf::Image /
  sf::SoundBuffer / sf::Music open their data from it (openFromStream).
  sfx::buildZip() writes a folder's files into a new archive, optionally
  with a password and a progress callback. Paths and entry names are UTF-8
  text (a PaskalCPP string) on every target; a path goes through SysUtils'
  ResolvePath, so it may start with $P: (the program's folder) or $D:.

  sfx::openFromResData() / loadFromResData() open an sf::Font / sf::Music /
  sf::Texture / sf::Image / sf::SoundBuffer from the program's built-in data
  (@addresdata, by key), the same on every target. sfml_ext builds a default
  font into every program that imports it: sfx::openDefaultFont().

  sfx::Video plays an MPEG-1 video with its MP2 audio (pl_mpeg) from a file,
  an sf::InputStream or a zip entry, as sf::Music plays a sound: play /
  pause / stop, looping, volume, a status callback; update() once a frame
  decodes by the real time passed, and it is drawn as any sf::Drawable.

  Errors: SFML's error reports (sf::err()) are caught from the program's
  start, one message per report. sfx::getLastError() gives the newest;
  sfx::setErrorCallback() sends every message to a routine instead of stderr
  (none set: stderr, as SFML does); sfx::setError() reports a program's own
  error, formatted as FormatStr does, the same way.

  Console (std\Console.pcpp) is imported here: an sf::Color reaches its
  colour routines as sfx::fromSf(AColor), as in
  SetForegroundColor(sfx::fromSf(sfx::Color::Gold)). sfx::messageBox()
  shows a modal message box with an OK button (Windows: the system's;
  Linux: an SFML window in the default font).

  sfx::Mixer is a sound manager over SFML audio, owned by the program: music
  streamed from a file, an sf::InputStream or a zip entry (play / pause /
  resume / stop, looping, offset, duration, fades), sounds decoded once and
  played as voices on a fixed set of channels (a free channel, a given one or
  the oldest voice of no higher priority; pitch, pan, looping, a 2D position
  with distance fading), reserved channels, a global pause that resumes only
  what it paused, and levels 0 to 1 (master, music, sounds, each music and
  voice) heard through Math's PerceivedVolume. Handles carry a generation, so
  a stale one changes nothing; loading what is loaded shares it, counted.
==============================================================================*/

module unit sfml_ext;

// The X11 headers a Linux build includes (Xft.dpi, the work area): vendor/linux64.
@ifdef TARGET_X86_64_WINDOWS_GNU
  @linklibrary "user32";
@elseif TARGET_X86_64_LINUX_GNU
  @addincludepath "$P:res/libs/vendor/linux64/include";
@else
  @message error "sfml_ext: unsupported target";
@endif

// The built-in default font (sfx::openDefaultFont): every program importing
// sfml_ext carries it, under the key sfx::DefaultFontKey.
@addresdata "sfml_ext/default_font" "$P:res/assets/fonts/JetBrainsMonoRegular.ttf";

import
  sfml,
  minizip,
  pl_mpeg,
  SysUtils,
  Console,
  Math,
  ResData;

// Public: the sfx types, SFML headers only. The OS headers stay in this unit's
// own source below (windows.h and Xlib.h define macros SFML's names clash with).
cpp header;

#include <cstddef>
#include <cstdint>
#include <format>
#include <functional>
#include <limits>
#include <memory>
#include <optional>
#include <span>
#include <string>
#include <string_view>
#include <vector>

namespace sfx
{

// Named colours, read as SFML's own (sf::Color::White): sfx::Color::AliceBlue.
// The CSS colours (both Gray and Grey spellings) plus Blank (transparent
// black), White2, Red22, ColorKey (magenta), Overlay1 / Overlay2, DimWhite,
// DarkSlateBrown and RayWhite; Transparent is transparent WHITE (a smooth
// texture's edge fades to white, not grey), sf::Color::Transparent is
// transparent black.
namespace Color
{

